    "type": "frame",
    "id": "342:422",
    "name": "Frame 91"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "342:428",
    "name": "Problem Space"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "342:429",
    "name": "Today&#39;s platforms are built for engagement, not meaningful relationships. Social media allows creators to build large communities but offers little control over personal interactions, while traditional dating apps prioritize discovery at scale over trust and compatibility. This creates a gap for creators who want to build genuine connections without compromising their privacy, and for users who seek authentic interactions beyond public comments and endless swiping. InfluCrush was conceived to bridge this gap by creating a relationship platform centered around trust, intentional access, and creator control."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "342:430",
    "name": "Frame 92"
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "342:434",
    "name": "Frame 100"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "342:432",
    "name": "Key Challenges"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "342:433",
    "name": "For Users Meaningful conversations are difficult to initiate in crowded social platforms, while traditional dating apps often encourage superficial interactions. For Creators Managing thousands of unsolicited messages makes it challenging to identify genuine connection requests while maintaining personal boundaries. For Existing Platforms Current products solve either audience engagement or matchmaking, but neither supports structured, trust-first relationships between creators and their communities."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "352:54",
    "name": "Frame 94"
  },
  {
    "type": "rounded-rectangle",
    "id": "352:60",
    "name": "Influcrush (8) 1"
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:62",
    "name": "Frame 95"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:64",
    "name": "Opportunity"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:65",
    "name": "The rise of the creator economy has changed how people build trust online, but meaningful interactions still happen through public comments or overcrowded inboxes. Existing dating platforms solve discovery, while social platforms solve reach. Neither is designed for intentional relationships between creators and their communities. InfluCrush explores the opportunity to bridge that gap by combining creator control, trust-first interactions, and a premium relationship experience."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:66",
    "name": "Frame 96"
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:70",
    "name": "Frame 101"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:76",
    "name": "Creator Economy"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:78",
    "name": "Creators need meaningful interactions not thousands of unsolicited messages."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:80",
    "name": "Frame 102"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:82",
    "name": "Intentional Relationships"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:83",
    "name": "Users value quality conversations over endless swiping."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:84",
    "name": "Frame 103"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:86",
    "name": "Creator Control"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:87",
    "name": "Creators decide who can connect, when, and under what conditions."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "354:88",
    "name": "Frame 104"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:90",
    "name": "Premium Access"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "354:91",
    "name": "Monetization becomes part of the experience instead of interrupting it."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "358:92",
    "name": "Frame 97"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "358:94",
    "name": "How I validated the opportunity"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "358:95",
    "name": "Competitive analysis of Tinder, Bumble, Instagram, and Hinge. Product teardown of onboarding, discovery, and messaging flows. Creator economy and subscription model research. Behavioral pattern analysis across social and dating platforms."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "358:99",
    "name": "Frame 98"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "358:101",
    "name": "Key Insights"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "358:102",
    "name": "Users value meaningful conversations over endless swiping. Creators need control over who can contact them. Trust should be established before conversations begin. Monetization works best when it enhances the experience, not interrupts it."
  },
  {
    "type": "frame",
    "id": "358:103",
    "name": "Frame 99"
  },
  {
